%% v1.3.2: restructured so Financial Exception reads as a parallel/independent side-effect,
%% never a workflow stage the transaction must pass through. Business rule is unchanged from
%% v1.3/v1.3.1 (CFO can approve with pending receipts; workflow continues regardless) — this is
%% a diagram-only correction, per the v1.3.2 change request item 5.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> SD_Mgmt_Pending: CRM requests Sale Deed Execution Approval\n(mandatory even for Direct Sale Deed, §43)

    SD_Mgmt_Pending --> Legal_Print_Pending: Management Approves\n(Management Approval #3 of 3)
    SD_Mgmt_Pending --> SD_Mgmt_Pending: Management Sends Back

    Legal_Print_Pending --> Legal_Manager_Check: Legal Executive prepares/prints,\nGarvi reference entered\n(v1.3.2: this print creates a documents row,\ntype SALE_DEED_PRINT, from this moment on — §1.4)

    Legal_Manager_Check --> CFO_Receipt_Check: Legal Manager Approves
    Legal_Manager_Check --> Legal_Print_Pending: Legal Manager Sends Back

    state CFO_Receipt_Check {
        [*] --> Checking_Components
        Checking_Components --> Checking_Components: Tick each component\nBasic / GST / Maint. / Deposit /\nStamp Duty / Legal / PNG / TDS\n+ Loan Cheque details
        Checking_Components --> [*]: CFO Approves\n(even with components still unticked)
    }

    state cfo_fork <<fork>>
    CFO_Receipt_Check --> cfo_fork: CFO Approves

    %% Main workflow path — this is the ONLY path the Sale Deed workflow itself follows.
    cfo_fork --> Customer_Signature_Pending: workflow ALWAYS continues here,\nregardless of receipt status (§48)

    %% Parallel, independent side-effect — NOT a workflow stage. financial_exceptions is its
    %% own state, tracked outside workflow_instances entirely (§1.5), closed independently
    %% whenever CFO later marks a component received — with no bearing on workflow progression.
    cfo_fork --> Financial_Exception_Open: IF any component was left\nunticked at approval (§48) —\na parallel/independent state,\nnot a stage of this workflow
    Financial_Exception_Open --> Financial_Exception_Resolved: Component later marked received\n(independent of workflow stage)
    Financial_Exception_Open --> Financial_Exception_Open: Notify CFO, Management, CRM\n(persists regardless of workflow progress, §50)

    Customer_Signature_Pending --> Legal_Final_Verification: CRM obtains customer signature

    Legal_Final_Verification --> SRO_Registration_Pending: Legal Manager final Approve
    Legal_Final_Verification --> Customer_Signature_Pending: Legal Manager Sends Back

    SRO_Registration_Pending --> Garvi_Downloads_Pending: Registration no., date,\nexecution date entered by Legal Executive\n(units.status → SALE_DEED_REGISTERED\nas soon as this happens — independent of\nwhat's below, and independent of any open\nfinancial exception, v1.3.2 §1.3a)

    Garvi_Downloads_Pending --> Admin_Scan_Pending: Legal Exec confirms\nIndex II + Certified Copy downloaded
    Garvi_Downloads_Pending --> Admin_Scan_Pending: OR Management Skip Permission\n(remark + audit, §54)

    Admin_Scan_Pending --> Admin_Scan_Pending: Blocked until Sales Close\nConfirmation ticked
    Admin_Scan_Pending --> CRMExec_Scan_Check: Admin confirms scan +\nAccounts copy + Sales Close\n(post-scan financial alert fires\nif exceptions still open, §52)

    CRMExec_Scan_Check --> Handover_Pending: CRM Exec marks Scan Verified

    Handover_Pending --> SaleDeed_Completed: Handover date + signed\nreceiving copy uploaded

    SaleDeed_Completed --> [*]: status_document = Completed.\nunits.status → COMPLETED only if zero OPEN\nfinancial_exceptions at this point, else\nFINANCIAL_EXCEPTION (v1.3.2 §1.3a) — the\nFinancial_Exception_Open state above may\nstill be unresolved here, and that's fine;\nit closes on its own timeline, not this one's.
